pySMESH: a chordal error limits the size on cylinder and torus faces again under OCCT 8
(NETGENPlugin V9_16_0; applies after NETGENPlugin_face_maxh_index.patch).

Defect: SetLocalSizeForChordalError reads a face's curvature with
Max( Abs( surfProp.MaxCurvature()), Abs( surfProp.MinCurvature() )) right after
surfProp.SetParameters(u, v), at three places. In OCCT 7, MaxCurvature() computed the
curvature first (LProp_SLProps.gxx: IsCurvatureDefined(), then return myMaxCurv). In
OCCT 8.0.1, BRepLProp_SLProps is GeomLProp_SLPropsBase<BRepAdaptor_Surface>, and
MaxCurvature() is RequireCurvature(*this, myMaxCurv): the cached value is copied into the
by-value argument before RequireCurvature calls IsCurvatureDefined()
(GeomLProp_SurfaceUtils.hxx:701, unchanged on OCCT master). So the first of the two reads
returns the curvature cached for the previous parameters, 0 on a fresh object, and only the
second is current. MSVC reads MinCurvature() first. For a cylinder, sphere or torus face
the plugin reads once, on a fresh object, and gets max(0, |MaxCurvature|): 0 for a
cylinder (curvatures 0 and -1/R), so an infinite size and no effect at all; the smaller
curvature for a torus, so a size too large; the right value for a sphere only because its
two curvatures are equal. Measured: a chordal error of 0.002 on a cylinder of radius 1 at
max_size 0.4 left the lateral face's mesh unchanged, mean triangle edge 0.411, largest
centroid deviation 0.031 (tests/test_mesher_netgen_face_size.py). On other curved faces
one of the two curvatures of each sample came from the sample before.

Change, in NETGENPlugin_Mesher.cxx only: one helper, maxCurvatureMagnitude(), calls
IsCurvatureDefined() before it reads the two curvatures, and throws LProp_NotDefined where
the curvature is not defined, as OCCT 7's MaxCurvature() did. The three reads call it. A
mesh with no chordal error does not change.

diff --git a/src/NETGENPlugin/NETGENPlugin_Mesher.cxx b/src/NETGENPlugin/NETGENPlugin_Mesher.cxx
